{"step_index":116,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-27T03:17:02Z","thinking":"**Observing DevTools' Display**\n\nI'm currently fixated on the user's DevTools window, specifically the tabs displayed: Elements, Sources, Network, Performance, Memory, Application. My focus has shifted; I wonder if interactions like key presses, pasting, or clicks are possible within this environment, particularly looking at the Elements tab now.\n\n\n**Analyzing Window Interaction**\n\nI'm now investigating potential interactions within the window, specifically focusing on the DreamCampus elements. I see the main body structure and the chat iframe. My goal is to find the \"Next\" button or controls, considering their possible placement in the bottom or navigation bar. I've noted the window size, 1536x863. I'm thinking of a script to focus the window, switch to the Console, and then potentially use key presses like `Escape` to toggle the drawer Console or send mouse clicks. Another idea involves sending keystrokes via `SendInput` or UIAutomation for control or even running an auto-next script.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"ArtifactMetadata":{"RequestFeedback":false,"Summary":"UI Automation element tree inspector for Dream Campus window","UserFacing":false},"CodeContent":"using System;\nusing System.Text;\nusing System.Runtime.InteropServices;\nusing System.Collections.Generic;\nusing System.Windows.Automation;\n\npublic class UIInspector {\n    [DllImport(\"user32.dll\", SetLastError = true)]\n    public static extern IntPtr OpenWindowStation(string lpszWinSta, bool fInherit, uint dwDesiredAccess);\n\n    [DllImport(\"user32.dll\", SetLastError = true)]\n    public static extern bool SetProcessWindowStation(IntPtr hWinSta);\n\n    [DllImport(\"user32.dll\", SetLastError = true)]\n    public static extern IntPtr OpenDesktop(string lpszDesktop, uint dwFlags, bool fInherit, uint dwDesiredAccess);\n\n    [DllImport(\"user32.dll\", SetLastError = true)]\n    public static extern bool SetThreadDesktop(IntPtr hDesktop);\n\n    public static void Attach() {\n        IntPtr hwinsta = OpenWindowStation(\"WinSta0\", false, 0x037F);\n        if (hwinsta != IntPtr.Zero) SetProcessWindowStation(hwinsta);\n        IntPtr hdesk = OpenDesktop(\"default\", 0, false, 0x01FF);\n        if (hdesk != IntPtr.Zero) SetThreadDesktop(hdesk);\n    }\n\n    public static void Inspect(IntPtr hWnd) {\n        Attach();\n        var element = AutomationElement.FromHandle(hWnd);\n        if (element == null) {\n            Console.WriteLine(\"Could not get AutomationElement from handle\");\n            return;\n        }\n\n        Console.WriteLine(\"Root: \" + element.Current.Name + \" (\" + element.Current.ControlType.ProgrammaticName + \")\");\n        PrintChildren(element, 0);\n    }\n\n    private static void PrintChildren(AutomationElement parent, int depth) {\n        if (depth > 6) return;\n        var cond = Condition.TrueCondition;\n        var children = parent.FindAll(TreeScope.Children, cond);\n        string indent = new string(' ', depth * 2);\n\n        foreach (AutomationElement child in children) {\n            try {\n                var name = child.Current.Name;\n                var ctype = child.Current.ControlType.ProgrammaticName;\n                var autoId = child.Current.AutomationId;\n                var rect = child.Current.BoundingRectangle;\n                if (!string.IsNullOrEmpty(name) || !string.IsNullOrEmpty(autoId) || ctype.Contains(\"Button\") || ctype.Contains(\"Edit\")) {\n                    Console.WriteLine(string.Format(\"{0}[{1}] Name: '{2}', Id: '{3}', Rect: ({4},{5},{6}x{7})\", \n                        indent, ctype.Replace(\"ControlType.\", \"\"), name, autoId, (int)rect.X, (int)rect.Y, (int)rect.Width, (int)rect.Height));\n                }\n                PrintChildren(child, depth + 1);\n            } catch {}\n        }\n    }\n}\n","Description":"UI Automation element inspector for Dream Campus window","Overwrite":true,"TargetFile":"C:\\Users\\lg\\.gemini\\antigravity\\brain\\44470555-939d-4160-8744-09bb2f099064\\scratch\\UIInspector.cs","toolAction":"Writing UIInspector.cs","toolSummary":"UI Inspector script"}}]}
